<title>USA: E-Z-EM gets FDA approval to market device.</title>
<headline>E-Z-EM gets FDA approval to market device.</headline>
<dateline>QUEENSBURY, N.Y. 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>E-Z-EM Inc said on Monday that its Angiodynamics Inc subsidiary had received permission from the U.S. Food and Drug Administration to market the company's Pulse Spray Injector.</p>
<p>The injector is self-contained and delivers therapeutic and blood clot dissolving drugs into a patient's body through a catheter, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>The device also maintains drug therapy while patients are being transported, or in the event of a power outage, the company said.</p>
</text>
